  "notes": "{濡|ぬ}らす is a godan verb meaning to wet or moisten something.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{濡|ぬ}れる→濡れる：00800_nureru⟧ (intransitive - to get wet)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{濡|ぬ}らす: to wet X\n- X⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{濡|ぬ}らす: to wet with X\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦タオル→タオル：01533_taoru⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{濡|ぬ}らす: to wet a towel\n- ⟦{髪|かみ}→髪：02196_kami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{濡|ぬ}らす: to wet one's hair\n- ⟦{唇|くちびる}→唇：03903_kuchibiru⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{濡|ぬ}らす: to moisten one's lips\n- ⟦{涙|なみだ}→涙：02235_namida⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧⟦{頬|ほお}→頬：03717_hoo⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{濡|ぬ}らす: to wet one's cheeks with tears\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n⟦{手|て}→手：00569_te⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{濡|ぬ}らさず⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧: without lifting a finger (lit. without wetting one's hands) - to achieve something without effort",
